# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows defaults core.autocrlf to true, so a shell script
# committed with LF is CHECKED OUT with CRLF - and bash then fails on the
# shebang line with "set: pipefail: invalid option name", which names
# neither the file nor the cause.
#
# Measured, not anticipated: tools/gates.sh, the local gate WORKFLOW.md
# tells every contributor to run to zero before pushing, could not run at
# all from the Windows working copy. It ran in CI, so the failure was
# invisible from the side that matters least. A gate that only the server
# can run is not a local gate.
#
# * text=auto normalises on the way in; the eol=lf lines below pin what
#   comes back out for the files where the ending is executable content
#   rather than presentation.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.cff       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf

# MATLAB and Markdown are read and written on Windows far more often than
# on Linux here, and nothing executes their line endings, so they follow
# the platform.
*.m         text
*.md        text
*.txt       text

# The GENERATED MANUAL, now that a clone is the delivery (D-020, PV-146).
# build_help writes LF; Git for Windows would check it back out as CRLF,
# and the next rebuild would write LF again - so every run would leave 47
# files modified and the tree permanently dirty. Pinned to LF so a
# rebuild that changes nothing changes nothing, which is what makes
# documentationSync's green mean something.
docs/html/**   text eol=lf

# MANIFEST.txt records a SHA-256 per file. Its own hashes are computed
# over the text as MATLAB reads it, so it must not be renormalised
# differently from the files it describes.
MANIFEST.txt text eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be touched.
*.mat       binary
*.mltbx     binary
*.png       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.b         binary
*.shp       binary
*.dbf       binary
*.shx       binary
